    "title": "Create a calm, cinematic lifestyle video centered around nature, greenery, and earthy living. The visual world blends modern urban life with the natural ecosystem—indoor plants, balconies full of greens, gardens, sunlight, wooden furniture, and clay textures.\n\nShow real urban adults (men and women, ages 25–35) using Dhara earthen bottles in everyday routines: working at a desk near plants, refilling the bottle in a garden or terrace, practicing yoga outdoors, and keeping the bottle beside the bed or dining table.\n\nFocus on close-up shots of the earthen bottle: the natural clay texture, water being poured slowly, condensation forming on the surface, hands holding the bottle, and calm facial expressions while drinking water.\n\nInclude short, natural dialogues and testimonial-style moments spoken directly to camera in a relaxed, honest tone:\n– “I wanted to stop using plastic, but I needed something practical.”\n– “Dhara just fits into my routine.”\n– “The quality feels premium and solid.”\n– “You can actually feel the difference in the water.”\n– “It cools naturally, without a fridge.”\n– “I’ve been using it every day—and it’s become a habit now.”\n\nLet the dialogues clearly communicate why people choose Dhara: natural cooling, plastic-free living, high-quality craftsmanship, and calm daily rituals.\n\nMaintain a warm, earthy color palette—terracotta tones, greens, browns, soft neutral light. Use natural ambient sounds like birds, wind, and water pouring. Keep pacing slow, minimal, and soothing.\n\nEnd with a soft but confident call-to-action on screen and voice-over:\n“Choose water that respects nature.”\n“Bring Dhara into your daily ritual.”\n\nClose with the Dhara logo and final line:\n“One small switch. Quality you can feel. A habit you’ll keep.”\n\nOverall mood: grounded, conscious, trustworthy, premium, and reassuring. Avoid loud music, fast cuts, or aggressive selling.",
